public class TicketRepository {
    @Transactional
    @Query("SELECT t FROM Ticket t WHERE t.id = :id AND t.status = 'AVAILABLE' FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED")
    public Optional<Ticket> lockAvailableTicket(@Param("id") Long id);
    // SKIP LOCKED is critical here. If 10,000 threads ask for tickets, they won't queue up blocking on one row.
}

try-catch fallback mechanics:
1. PaymentTimeoutException: User closes browser mid-payment. The Redis TTL expires naturally after 5 minutes restoring the seat. 
2. DoubleChargeException: Server crashes right after Stripe replies. We must use an Idempotency Key (UUID generated by client at checkout) so submitting the retry doesn't charge the card twice.
